### 2. Research Profile Website Created
Built a clean, professional static site with 4 pages:

| Page | Content |
|------|---------|
| **Home** (`index.html`) | Hero section, brief bio, research interests grid, selected publications, latest blog posts, contact cards |
| **About** (`about.html`) | Full bio, education timeline, research interests, project cards, teaching/mentorship, skills grid, contact |
| **Publications** (`publications.html`) | Numbered publication list with highlighted author names, research interests, contact |
| **Blog** (`blog.html`) | Blog post cards with dates, excerpts, and tags, research interests, contact |

**Design features:**
- Professional dark blue color scheme with serif headings
- Responsive layout with mobile hamburger menu
- CSS custom properties for easy theming
- Print-friendly styles
- SVG icons (no external dependencies)
- Smooth transitions and hover effects

### 3. Git Commands to Push to GitHub
Run these commands from the `my_website/` directory:

```bash
# Add the remote (replace with your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/my_website.git

# Push to main branch (triggers the fixed deploy workflow)
git push -u origin main

# The GitHub Actions workflow will then:
# 1. Checkout the code
# 2. Install dependencies (npm ci)
# 3. Build the site (npm run build → outputs to ./public)
# 4. Deploy to GitHub Pages (peaceiris/actions-gh-pages)
```

The workflow will automatically run on push to `main`, building the site and deploying it to GitHub Pages on the `gh-pages` branch.

